.g., Pure Shifted Chows), but we lack supporting tiles. Holding multiple from same chow risks inefficiency.\n- Best candidates for discard: **F1**, **B1**, or **B3**\u2014least likely to contribute.\n\nBut note: I previously played **T8, T1, B2, B6, B4, F4, W5, J1/J2/J3**, indicating active discarding of honors and scattered suited tiles. Opponents have revealed many middle tiles (T4-T8, W5-W7), suggesting congestion in central ranges.\n\nReason: Given the lack of connectivity in hand and scarcity of surrounding tiles, the priority is efficiency\u2014shedding least useful tiles. **F1** is an honor tile not matching seat (East) or prevailing (South) wind, and there's no sign of building an honor-based pattern. It cannot form a pung easily (only 3 unshown, likely distributed). Keeping it blocks progress. Among all options, **F1** offers the least potential for future melds or scoring patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play F1"}
