ll isolated tiles with limited synergy.\n\nI am far from major patterns like Full Flush, All Honors, or Four Pungs. Best feasible paths include Outside Hand (if I keep terminals/honors), Mixed Triple Chow (unlikely), or Chicken Hand (default 8-point base). Currently, I lack four clear melds/pairs; I have two melds and eight loose tiles.\n\nBest chance is building toward **Outside Hand** (8 points) by keeping terminal and honor tiles. Alternatively, aim for **All Types** (6 points) which requires at least one of each category.\n\nReason: Among valid discards, **B3** is the weakest connector. It would require B1/B2 for a chow, but B2 has only one left and was recently played by opponent (across player played B2 twice), suggesting danger. Also, B1 is low frequency. B3 itself offers no pung potential (only three B3s left, none in my hand beyond this one). Compared to safer honors like J3 (only one unseen), B3 contributes less to scoring patterns and poses slightly higher risk of enabling a lower-chow hand for someone else.\n\nThus, **Play B3** minimizes risk while preserving more flexible honor tiles and avoiding cluttering the hand with weak connectors.\n\nAnswer: Play B3"}
